SWEET CHG SOC (patch 0307, ALL-ON goal, user 2026-11-11 "can't you literally read the battery percentage?"): the SWEET CHG P3 rows (patch 0287) and the 30 s SWEET CHG MON rows (patch 0298) also read the fuel gauge's RepSOC (0x36 register 0x06, 2 bytes low first, LSB 1/256 %) and print 'soc=NN.NN %' after vcell; the MON rows also read the gauge Temp (0x08, signed 1/256 C, battery thermistor; src BMS 6702fca8 max_m5.c:1593, max_m5_reg.h:219, max1720x_battery.c:526-530) and print 'temp=NN.N C' (a heat signal: an all-on boot reset with no log at max clocks, resident-184344-b1), so the host battery floor uses the gauge's charge state instead of the loaded VCell (session 20261111T182314Z parked a 72.48 % phone at a loaded 3676 mV). Same chip, same transfer and conversion as the phase-2 RepSOC read of i2c_g_fg (patch 0284, research charger-max77759-gs101.md note 2 from BMS max1720x_battery.h / max_m5_reg.h). The fuel-gauge read allowlist (patch 0284, i2c_rd_slave_ok) gains Temp 0x08 for the MON read (without it the compiler proved the MON row unreachable: kernel allon-k4 had no SWEET CHG MON string and every row would have failed). READS ONLY: no new chip or controller register written. Needs patch 0298.
